<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asilah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arzila</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asilah, historically Arzila, is a fortified town on the Atlantic coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a>. Portugal captured it in 1471 under Afonso V and held it until 1550, and King Sebastian landed there in 1578 before his defeat at Alcácer Quibir. Its Portuguese ramparts still enclose the old medina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asilah.jpg" alt="Asilah" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Prazeres · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asilah_seafront.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
